  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nhttps://wpt.fyi/results/html/semantics/forms/the-input-element/color.window.html?label=master&label=experimental&aligned&q=color.window.html\n\nIn \"Testing '#ffffff08' with color space 'limited-srgb' and with alpha (setAttribute(\"value\"))\", the test does:\n\n1. setAttribute(\"value\", color)\n2. Expects value is set as alpha-less hex\n3. Set .alpha = true\n4. Expect the alpha value revives\n\nBut https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#update-a-color-well-control-color overwrites the element value, so alpha value goes away per the spec. WebKit seems to use the attribute as long as the value is not [dirty](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-fe-dirty). Probably the algorithm should do the same.",
